            <ArticleTitle>Generation of 1/f noise from a broken-symmetry model for the arbitrary absolute pitch of musical melodies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>EL490</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1121/1.5011150</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A model is presented to generate power spectrum noise with intensity proportional to 1/f  as a function of frequency f. The model arises from a broken-symmetry variable, which corresponds to absolute pitch, where fluctuations occur in an attempt to restore that symmetry, influenced by interactions in the creation of musical melodies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
